PW PBE0 AFM Fe with uneven k-point pools.

The two Fe atoms in a 3.5 Angstrom bcc cell start with opposite moments.
Fixed occupations keep equal populations in the two spin channels; no
local magnetic-moment constraint is imposed. The converged state has
negligible total moment and an absolute moment of about 6.53481 mu_B
per cell. A diagnostic nearest-atom spin-density partition gives finite,
opposite Fe moments (about -3.2 and +3.2 mu_B), distinguishing AFM from NM.

Three k points per spin and kpar=2 exercise the idle target pool in both
spin channels. Run with an even number of MPI ranks, at least two; the
CPU suite uses four. The unfixed EXX implementation fails with
MPI_ERR_TRUNCATE. The energy reference was generated with kpar=1 and
four ranks. No new CTest entry is needed: CASES_CPU.txt is consumed by
the existing 01_PW integration test.

magnetism.ref opts into a total/absolute moment check at 1e-3 mu_B per
cell. The energy tolerance is 1e-4 eV because the deliberately loose
exx_ene_thr=0.05 Ry leaves differences of a few 1e-5 eV between pool
layouts. The 12 Ry cutoff and sparse mesh serve a fast regression, not
a cutoff/k-point convergence study. The existing FM companion checks
forces; this AFM case focuses on EXX energy and magnetic state.
